{{ define "custom_memory.tmpl" }}
{{ range .Alerts }}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>High Memory Alert</title>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:30px;font-family:'Segoe UI', Tahoma, sans-serif;background:#ffffff;color:#333;">
  <h2 style="color:#e63946;">High Memory Usage Detected</h2>

  <p style="font-size:16px;">
    <strong style="color:#1d3557;">{{ .Labels.instance }}</strong> has sustained high memory usage of
    <strong style="color:#e76f51;">{{ .Annotations.memory_usage }}%</strong> for over 10 minutes.
  </p>

  <p style="font-size:15px;">💻 <strong>Server Name:</strong> {{ .Labels.instance }}</p>
  <p style="font-size:15px;">📊 <strong>Current Usage:</strong> {{ .Annotations.memory_usage }}%</p>
  <p style="margin-top:20px;font-size:15px;">
  ⚙️ <strong>Action Required:</strong> Analyze memory consumption and identify high-usage processes:
  <br><br>
  🧾 <code>free -h</code><br>
  🧾 <code>top -o %MEM</code><br>
  🧾 <code>ps aux --sort=-%mem | head</code>
  <br><br>
  🧹 <strong>Optional (Clear Memory Cache):</strong><br>
  📌 <code>sync; echo 1 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches</code> – Clears page cache only<br>
  📌 <code>sync; echo 2 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches</code> – Clears dentries and inodes<br>
  📌 <code>sync; echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches</code> – Clears page cache, dentries, and inodes
  <br><br>
  ⚠️ <strong>Note:</strong> Use cache clearing commands cautiously in production environments. Monitor post-execution memory behavior.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size:12px;color:#999;margin-top:40px;">
    🚨 This is an automated alert from Alertmanager.
  </p>
</body>
</html>
{{ end }}
{{ end }}

